-labs/crypto/issues/events{/number}","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/issues{/number}","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/keys{/key_id}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/labels{/name}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/languages","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/merges","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/notifications{?since,all,participating}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/pulls{/number}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/releases{/id}","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/stargazers","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/statuses/{sha}","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/subscription","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/tags","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/teams","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/git/trees{/sha}"},"score":1.0,"text_matches":[{"object_url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/contents/research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/verdicts/MP-symmetry-2.refute.json?ref=12a2b3d85f1796a9e793b7206763691e994012cd","object_type":"FileContent","property":"content","fragment":"{\"idea_id\":\"MP-symmetry-2\",\"skeptic_lens\":\"mathematical refutation\",\"verdict\":\"survives_with_fix\",\"confidence\":0.75,\n\"reason\":\"(1) Arm P/H2 ill-posed: Weil descent of S_4 from F_{p^3} with x in F_p gives 3 polys in 3 unknowns over F_p WITHOUT field equations (x^p-x has degree p>=101 >> c<=24). Generic square system => zero-dim nonempty variety over F_pbar regardless of F_p-rational SAT/UNSAT, so 1 never in W_c: c_1 = infinity for both sat and unsat targets; UNSAT is invisible to Macaulay rank at c<=24. Delta in ideal iff every F_pbar solution lies on a diagonal x_i=x_j, non-generic; so c_Delta<c_1 prediction is untestable/false by dimension count. (2) H1 at solving level is tautological: 1 is G-invariant, so 1 in W_c iff 1 in P_triv W_c holds for any G-stable subspace (Reynolds projector, char not dividing |G|) - no information about d_F growth. (3) Isotypic split of ranks is an exact accounting identity (dim W_c = sum of block dims), it cannot by itself bound any exponent; per-block deficit proportions say nothing about lever-1 complexity. (4) Binary arm algebra is correct: F_2[Z/3]=F_2 x F_4, rank_chi over F_4 = (rank_full - rank_triv)/2 over F_2. (5) Non-genericity: uses polynomial representation (not a generic-group algorithm), so CGK does not apply, but also no algorithmic gain claimed.\",\n\"fix\":\"Drop Arm P and H2 (or add field equations, which requires c>=p and kills the toy range). Keep Arm Z only (binary, field equations included so 1 in ideal is meaningful) as an accounting note: record which Z/3 block carries the rank deficit vs n; no lever claim.\",\n\"file\":\"/Users/adamburan/ic-work/crypto/research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/verdicts/MP-symmetry-2.refute.json\",\n\"collisions\":[\"TREAT-first-fall-degree-constant\",\"THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1\"]}","matches":[{"text":"THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1","indices":[1743,1764]}]}]},{"name":"MP-additive_comb-1.collision.json","path":"research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/verdicts/MP-additive_comb-1.collision.json","sha":"a94e3bf69ce90f68d65df90af19cd5fadb3ad122","url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/contents/research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/verdicts/MP-additive_comb-1.collision.json?ref=12a2b3d85f1796a9e793b7206763691e994012cd","git_url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/git/blobs/a94e3bf69ce90f68d65df90af19cd5fadb3ad122","html_url":"https://github.com/isogeny-labs/crypto/blob/12a2b3d85f17