ion_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/subscription","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/tags","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/teams","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/git/trees{/sha}"},"score":1.0,"text_matches":[{"object_url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/contents/research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/verdicts/MP-additive_comb-1.collision.json?ref=12a2b3d85f1796a9e793b7206763691e994012cd","object_type":"FileContent","property":"content","fragment":"{\"idea_id\":\"MP-additive_comb-1\",\"skeptic_lens\":\"prior-art and closure collision\",\"verdict\":\"survives_with_fix\",\"confidence\":0.6,\n\"reason\":\"No source states a 2-valued/multiset-filter Wagner variant (2 WebSearch extended: Kummer/Wagner/x-only pseudo-addition; only Montgomery pseudo-addition, Semaev S_m, Wagner 2002 returned; no combination). But it is a near-duplicate of open KN-OPEN-91d4f6 and is reduced to it: h is a function of x so h(-Q)=h(Q) and h(P-Q)=h(P+(-Q)); both branches are the same single-valued correlation (same character sums T_t of KN-FIND-ffe1df) so a 2-valued bucket gain G2 <= ~2G, and the 2x/level cost is already paid; G2 grows iff G grows. Claimed wall bypass (not a homomorphism to a quotient) is already the premise of 91d4f6 (non-group filter), so it is not a new door. Falsifier domain traps: on prime-order <P> the F_2 trace filter is constant (gain 1) and exact gain h only on E(F_{2^n}) (KN-OPEN-91d4f6 Known; sampling domain load-bearing); TREAT-wagner-klist and THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1 cover x-type degree-2 quotient symmetry; LEAD-EXO-curve-model-representation closed_obstructed (Kummer line Bezout-optimal). Prime-field x mod M / floor(xM/p) arm falls under KN-FIND-ffe1df character-sum level-1 bound and exhausted coordinate-statistic bias hunts. Level>=2 tree not closed by level-1 bound.\",\n\"fix\":\"Restate as a corollary experiment of KN-OPEN-91d4f6: G2 vs G on the same data; sample Q,R from the prime-order subgroup <P> only (not E(F_{2^n}), not F_p trace); include the trace-constant control; drop the claim of bypassing Theorem C; expected_class theory/null. Uncovered part: only the formal 2-valued extension and level>=2 multiset composition.\",\n\"collisions\":[\"KN-OPEN-91d4f6 (open; same filter family, single-valued)\",\"KN-FIND-ffe1df (Theorem C exact-filter nonexistence; level-1 character-sum bound)\",\"TREAT-wagner-klist (scope leaves non-group filter open)\",\"THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1 (x-type quotient symmetry)\",\"LEAD-EXO-curve-model-representation (closed_obstructed; Kummer line Bezout-optimal)\",\"Wagner 2002; Montgomery/Kummer pseudo-addition (background only)\"],\n\"file\":\"/Users/adamburan/ic-work/crypto/research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/verdicts/MP-additive_comb-1.collision.json\"}","matches":[{"text":"THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1","indices":[998,1019]},{"text":"THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1","indices":[1906,1927]}]}]},{"name":"companion_catalogue.tex","path":"papers/ecdlp-index-calculus-program/sections/companion_catalogue.tex","sha":"2bb7712687c168ea462fd37ec342cdde592f9616","url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/contents/papers/ecdlp-index-calculus-program/sections/companion_catalogue.tex?ref=12a2b3d85f1796a9e793b7206763691e994012cd","git_url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/git/blobs/2bb7712687c168ea462fd37ec342cdde592f9616","html_url":"https://github.com/isogeny-labs/crypto/blob/12a2b3d85f1796a9e793b7206763691e994012cd/papers/ecdlp-index-calculus-program/sections/companion_catalogue.tex","repository":{"id":1221029056,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnkxMjIxMDI5MDU2","name":"crypto","full_name":"isogeny-labs/crypto","owner":{"id":347052081,"node_id":"O_kgDOFK-YMQ","login":"isogeny-labs","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/347052081?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/isogeny-labs","html_url":"https://github.com/isogeny-labs","type":"Organization","site_admin":false,