tors{/collaborator}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/comments{/number}","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/commits{/sha}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/compare/{base}...{head}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/contents/{+path}","contributors_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/contributors","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/deployments","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/downloads","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/events","forks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/forks","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/git/commits{/sha}","git_refs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/git/refs{/sha}","git_tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/git/tags{/sha}","hooks_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/hooks","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/issues/comments{/number}","issue_events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/issues/events{/number}","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/issues{/number}","keys_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/keys{/key_id}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/labels{/name}","languages_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/languages","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/merges","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/notifications{?since,all,participating}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/pulls{/number}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/releases{/id}","stargazers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/stargazers","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/statuses/{sha}","subscribers_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/subscribers","subscription_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/subscription","tags_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/tags","teams_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/teams","trees_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/isogeny-labs/crypto/git/trees{/sha}"},"score":1.0,"text_matches":[{"object_url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/contents/research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/ideas/symmetry.json?ref=12a2b3d85f1796a9e793b7206763691e994012cd","object_type":"FileContent","property":"content","fragment":"      \"wall_bypassed\": \"TREAT-first-fall-degree-constant (open side: 'whether d_F grows without bound is open; proof route suggested: degree-c pseudo-solutions'); TREAT-summation-cover-monodromy (closes fibre censuses and yield, leaves solving difficulty free); KN-OPEN-8f3d27/-3c8f51. Also positioned against the adjacent_fields.json suggestion 'ideas/isotypic_pseudosolutions' (S_3-isotypic decomposition, test whether the sign component carries the growth) - which this idea subsumes with two added mechanisms.\",\n      \"why_wall_hypotheses_fail\": \"The closures concern WHAT d_F is (presentation-dependent, unknown growth) and never used representation theory to organise the certificate space; the monodromy closure is about Galois fibres of the summation cover, not about the S_m-module structure of the Macaulay matrix. New mechanisms over the corpus suggestion: (1) the Specht/Vandermonde containment degree c_Delta as a measurable invariant separating 'diagonal' from 'off-diagonal' pseudo-solutions (THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1 / FGHR remove the diagonal by invariant-ring rewriting; this measures whether the solver's remaining degrees are spent there); (2) the binary Z/3 instance via rank differences (no F_4 arithmetic), giving the only non-modular isotypic split available over F_2 for a summand-permutation symmetry; (3) per-block semi-regular nulls computed from random G-symmetrised systems.\",\n      \"nongenericity_argument\": \"None directly: theory. It cannot lower B*D^2; it can decide which block a lever-1 proof must address. If H1 holds with the trivial block carrying the fall, then the uniform-in-n pseudo-solution route reduces to functionals on orbit sums (n-independent index set for the barrel, 3-fold smaller for Z/3) - a proof of d_F >= 5 for all n (kills subexponential heuristics) or a bounded f(m) (revives them) would be an exponent-level statement, but it is a consequence of a future proof, not of this experiment.\",\n      \"prior_art\": \"Moustrou-Riener-Verdure, 'Symmetric ideals, Specht polynomials and solutions to symmetric systems of equations' (arXiv:1912.05266); Breloer-Riener, 'Symmetric and isotypic Hilbert series for symmetric ideals' (arXiv:2606.18895); Debus-Gottwald, Specht ideals for dihedral/type-D reflection groups (arXiv:2506.15335); Gorla-Trebiani, 'Symmetric models for syndrome decoding' (arXiv:2609.14052; proved d_reg of an S_n-symmetric Boolean ideal by Hilbert-function counting); Faugere-Gaudry-Huot-Renault 2014 (invariant-ring rewriting); programme: THM_SEMAEV_FALL1 (attribution of falls to Frobenius/symmetry syzygies), THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1 (translation group (Z/2)^{m-1} x| S_m), fpn_degrees.py system_labels (exact degree labels over F_{p^n}). adjacent_fields.json sublane 6 proposes the S_3-isotypic split; the Specht-containment degree and the binary Z/3 rank-difference arm are not in the corpus (grep of MAP_ideas_corpus.json for 'Specht', 'isotypic', 'Vandermonde': 0 cards).\",\n      \"novelty_status\": \"novelty_unverified (no web search; literature lane confirms no programme card uses Specht/isotypic structure; the Specht-containment-degree invariant as a solving-degree diagnostic was not searched)\",\n      \"falsifier\": {\n        \"design\": \"Arm P (prime field, S_3 full isotypic): E/F_{p^3} with base {x in F_p}, p in {101, 211, 401, 1009} (p != 2,3 so projectors exist), m=3 unsymmetrised: S_4(x1,x2,x3,x_R) from csd.semaev.S4() specialised to (a,b) over F_{p^3} (fpn_degrees.GF(p,3)); x_i are F_p-scalars so the Weil descent is just the 3 F_p-coordinates of the F_{p^3}-valued polynomial: 3 polynomials in 3 unknowns, total degree <= 12. Append field equations x_i^p - x_i only for the ground truth (solutions = F_p-points); for degree labels use the Macaulay matrix of the 3 polynomials at degrees c = 12..24 (columns C(3+c,3) <= 2925). For 16 unsat and 8 sat targets: per degree, rank of the full matrix and of P_lambda-projected matrices for lambda in {triv, sign, std} (projectors over F_p via the 6 permutation matrices on monomial exponents), compared with the same quantities for a null of random S_3-symmetrised cubic-by-cubic systems of equal degree profile; record c_1 = min{c: 1 in W_c} and c_Delta = min{c : Delta in W_c} (Delta = (x1-x2)(x1-x3)(x2-x3), degree 3), and the dimension of the cokernel per block at c_1 - 1. Arm Z (binary Z/3 via ranks): reuse MP-symmetry-1 Arm A output (n=11,13,17,19,23; l=4; 8 unsat targets): rank_chi(c) = (rank_full(c) - rank_triv(c))/2 per degree, its deficit against the null (random Z/3-symmetrised Boolean sextics with the same number of components), and the cokernel split dim(coker_triv), dim(coker_chi) at c*-1 as a function of n at fixed l.\",","matches":[{"text":"THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1","indices":[1008,1029]},{"text":"THM_QUOTIENT_DESCENT1","indices":[2580,2601]}]}]},{"name":"MAP_ideas_corpus.json","path":"research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/brief/MAP_ideas_corpus.json","sha":"f3c894d19c35a50ebef7b59c87544f85c532973c","url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/contents/research/ic_mega_pass_20261031/brief/MAP_ideas_corpus.json?ref=12a2b3d85f1796a9e793b7206763691e994012cd","git_url":"https://api.github.com/repositories/1221029056/git/blobs/f3c894